    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.starter\n\n### Description\n\nWhen opening the `mini.starter`, either on `VimEnter` or manually, on the default settings, Neovim hangs irrecoverably.\r\n\r\nProbably caused by 32cb2b23805a?\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNeovim nightly v0.9.0-dev-594+gc590641fe commit neovim/neovim@c590641febf4d03e89c46f8e7ef4c3fb2a455520\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nMinimal `init.lua`:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath 'data' .. '/lazy/lazy.nvim'\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n    vim.fn.system {\r\n        'git',\r\n        'clone',\r\n        '--filter=blob:none',\r\n        '--single-branch',\r\n        'https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git',\r\n        lazypath,\r\n    }\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.runtimepath = { lazypath }\r\n\r\nrequire('lazy').setup { {\r\n    'echasnovski/mini.nvim',\r\n    config = function()\r\n        require 'mini.starter'.setup {}\r\n    end,\r\n} }\r\n```\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n\r\n-- OR --\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('lazy').setup {\r\n    'echasnovski/mini.nvim',\r\n}\r\nrequire'mini.starter'.setup {\r\n    autoopen = false,\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. `:lua MiniStarter.open()`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nMiniStarter opens normally with the default settings\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nNeovim hangs completely, even doing a Ctrl-C doesn't help.",
