            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@folke, yeah this might be the case. I just saw newest Neovim version and remembered this 'noice.nvim' issue. Probably, they both have similar upstream root cause.\r\n\r\n@dtomvan, since I can not reproduce this, when you are back at the original machine could you try the following:\r\n- Latest 'mini.starter' but earlier Neovim version (0.8.2 or at most https://github.com/neovim/neovim/commit/99cf111289bfcd14981255e805da43bac5139141). If issue goes away, then it is a Neovim nightly release. Will wait for some time and see progress on Neovim. Ideally, finding minimal reproducible example and filing an upstream issue is better. \r\n- Latest Neovim but earlier 'mini.starter' version (before 32cb2b23805a52c75795792a2076a46a8d235486). If issue goes away, could you try replacing [this line](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/06eddfd8d6341e6c4f53ec9ae109a376a566329d/lua/mini/starter.lua#L1284) with `vim.schedule(function() vim.api.nvim_input([[<C-\\><C-n>]]) end)` and try again?",
