            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> @echasnovski When I'm using the minimal init.lua (I also tried it with packer.nvim, just to be sure) I'm only installing mini.starter, right?\r\n\r\nShould be true, yes. I am yet to study the difference between how 'lazy.nvim', 'packer.nvim', and built-in packages find what to load. There might be cases that plugin was installed in some place from where user forgot to remove it, thus it was loaded even when not asking explicitly. So it was just to be sure.\r\n\r\n> Huh. After rebooting (next use after yesterday) of the machine I reported this issue on, it just went away. I am sorry for bothering you with this. I have no idea how the issue might've came up, since I just can't reproduce it at all anymore.\r\n\r\nNo problem. There is some increased instability in Neovim nightly, though. I just tried to use it to run some tests and it indeed shows some \"hanging\" behavior. Interactively it works almost without changes. So yeah, I would restrain from using Neovim nightly for some time.\r\n\r\nClosing this, then. If you ever encounter it again, please, try to find reproducible steps and feel free to post/reopen.",
